    "difficultyReason": "The student does one distance calculation (a 3-4-5 case), then reads AB:BC=2:3 as BC=3/2·AB. Finally they add AB and BC for AC, with 'Hence' signposting each step. This needs one interpretation of the ratio and a short linked chain, with no coordinate division or hidden insight. It is harder than the single-step endpoint reversal in p6-q4, and easier than p7-q8, which requires fractions of both coordinate differences and an algebraic coordinate find.",
